<title>HONG KONG: Deutsche Bank sets call warrants on H-share basket.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank sets call warrants on H-share basket.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutshche Bank AG, London Branch, said on Friday it intended to issue 1,038 million American-style call warrants on a basket of eight locally-listed Chinese</p>
<p>enterprises H-shares.</p>
<p>Each basket comprises of:</p>
<p> Shanghai Petrochemical Co Ltd		 0.25 shares</p>
<p> Anhui Expressway Co Ltd			 0.13 shares</p>
<p> Maanshan Iron and Steel Co Ltd		0.26 shares</p>
<p> Jilin Chemical Industrial Co Ltd	    0.23 shares</p>
<p> Yizheng Chemical Fibre Co Ltd		 0.23 shares</p>
<p>Guangdong Kelon Electrical Holdings Co Ltd 0.05 shares</p>
<p> Guangshen Railway Co Ltd			0.08 shares</p>
<p> Qingling Motors Ltd			     0.07 shares</p>
<p>Ten warrants control one basket.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE	HK$2.7826	PREMIUM	 19 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	 HK$0.0897	GEARING	 3.45x</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	  03.APR.98	EXER LOT	10,000</p>
<p> LISTING	     HONG KONG	PAYMENT DATE  13.JAN.97</p>
<p> REFERENCE SPOT    HK$3.0918	LISTING DATE  15.JAN 97</p>
<p> NOTE		  CASH SETTLEMENT OR PHYSICAL DELIVERY AT</p>
<p>			 DISCRETION OF ISSUER</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
